---
import {cities, nearbyAreas, localCopy} from '../data/cities';
import type {Scenario} from '../data/cities';
import DealForm from './DealForm.astro';
interface Props { cityName:string; intro:string; angle:string; caution:string; location:string; showCityGrid?:boolean; slug?:string; scenario?:Scenario; }
const {cityName,intro,angle,caution,location,showCityGrid=false,slug,scenario}=Astro.props;
const local = slug ? localCopy[slug] : undefined;
const metro = cityName === 'Tampa Bay';
const nearby = slug && nearbyAreas[slug] ? nearbyAreas[slug].map(s=>cities.find(c=>c.slug===s)).filter(Boolean) : [];
---
<section class="hero" id="main"><div class="container hero__inner"><div class="hero__content"><h1>Fix and flip loans <em>{metro ? 'across Tampa Bay' : `in ${cityName}, Florida`}</em></h1><div class="hero__rule"></div><a class="text-link" href="#how-it-works">See how the connection works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><DealForm cityName={cityName} location={location} /></div></section>
<div class="trust-bar"><div class="container trust-bar__inner"><span>Funding within 48 hours is our goal</span><span>Asset-based focus</span><span>Clear next steps</span></div></div>
<section class="section" id="local-market"><div class="container split"><div><p>{intro}</p><h2>{metro ? 'A project starts with the property' : local?.heading || `A closer look at ${cityName}`}</h2><p>{angle}</p><p>{caution}</p></div><aside class="side-note"><span class="side-note__mark" aria-hidden="true">↗</span><h3>{local ? 'Before choosing the scope' : 'Start with the actual deal'}</h3><p>{local?.check || 'Include the purchase contract, the scope of work and how you plan to sell. Funding sources can then look at the project on its own merits.'}</p></aside></div></section>
<section class="section section--tint" id="your-goal"><div class="container"><h2>Tell Us Your Goal</h2><p class="section__intro">Answer a few quick questions about your business and funding needs. We are connectors: we take what you tell us and introduce your project to funding sources that fit it.</p><div class="card-grid"><article><h3>What are you buying?</h3><p>{local ? `Identify the ${cityName} block, property type and lot. Include the contract and describe the existing layout before discussing what it could become.` : 'Give us the address or the neighborhood, the type of home and where the purchase stands.'}</p></article><article><h3>What will you do to it?</h3><p>{local?.scope || 'Describe the repairs and upgrades you have planned and who will do the work.'}</p></article><article><h3>How will you exit?</h3><p>{local?.comps || 'Tell us when you expect to close, finish and sell, and who the likely buyer is.'}</p></article></div><p class="section__intro" style="margin-top:22px">Ready? <a href="#deal-form">Send your project</a> and we will take it from there.</p></div></section>
<section class="section" id="why-us"><div class="container"><h2>Funding within 48 hours</h2><p class="section__intro">{local ? `A complete ${cityName} file includes the local checks behind your plan. ${local.check} Identify what is confirmed and what is still open so our funding conversation does not depend on an unchecked assumption.` : 'Speed comes from a complete package. Investors who send the contract, the repair scope and a supported resale estimate give funding sources what they need to respond quickly.'} The <a href="/fix-and-flip-project-checklist/">project checklist</a> lists exactly what to have ready, and the <a href="/fix-and-flip-vs-hard-money/">fix and flip vs hard money</a> guide explains how this kind of funding fits.</p><div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare-table"><caption class="sr-only">What to have ready for a fix and flip project</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Have ready</th><th scope="col">Why it helps</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Purchase contract or offer</th><td>Shows the property, the seller and the closing timeline</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Written repair scope</th><td>Lets a funding source see what the work involves</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Recent nearby sales</th><td>Supports your estimate of the finished home's value</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Photos of the property</th><td>Shows condition that a listing may not</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Your exit plan</th><td>Explains how and when the property will sell</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="term-disclosure">Timing depends on the project, the documents and the funding source. A submission is not an approval or a guarantee of funding.</p></div></section>
<section class="section section--dark" id="how-it-works"><div class="container"><h2>How the connection works</h2><p class="section__intro">The steps are the same in every town we serve. The full process is in our guide to <a href="/how-fix-and-flip-funding-works-in-florida/">how fix and flip funding works in Florida</a>.</p><div class="step-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Send the project</h3><p>{local ? `Send the ${cityName} address, photos and scope. Identify which exterior changes, site questions or prior alterations still need confirmation.` : 'Tell us about the property, your purchase and the work you plan. Flag anything that still needs confirmation.'}</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>We make the connection</h3><p>{local ? `We review the repair plan and resale support, then make a funding introduction. Explain why the selected local sales fit this house rather than just sharing a finished-value target.` : 'We review what you sent, ask for anything missing and introduce the project to funding sources that fit it.'}</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Review what comes back</h3><p>The funding source decides eligibility and documentation. Read the full written offer before you decide whether to move forward.</p></article></div></div></section>
{scenario && <section class="section scenario" id="local-example"><div class="container"><h2>{scenario.title}</h2><p class="section__intro">{scenario.intro}</p><ol class="scenario__list">{scenario.items.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ol><p class="scenario__outro" set:html={scenario.outro}/></div></section>}
<section class="section section--tint" id="faq"><div class="container faq"><h2>Questions before you submit</h2><div>{local?.faqs.map(f=><details><summary>{f.q}</summary><p>{f.a}</p></details>)}<details><summary>Are you a direct lender?</summary><p>No. We are connectors. We introduce investors to funding sources, and the funding source makes its own decisions and provides the actual terms.</p></details><details><summary>Does submitting a project guarantee funding?</summary><p>No. A submission starts a review and a possible introduction. It does not guarantee a match, an approval or a particular outcome.</p></details></div></div></section>
{showCityGrid && <section class="section section--tint" id="service-areas"><div class="container"><h2>Explore Tampa Bay</h2><p class="section__intro">Every property deserves a local look. Find your town below, then share the details of your project.</p><div class="city-grid">{cities.map(c=><a href={`/${c.slug}/`}><span>{c.county} County</span><strong>{c.name}</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div></div></section>}
{nearby.length>0 && <section class="nearby" aria-label="Nearby service areas"><div class="container"><h2 class="nearby__title">Nearby service areas</h2><ul class="nearby__list">{nearby.map(c=><li><a href={`/${c.slug}/`}>{c.name}, FL</a></li>)}</ul></div></section>}
<section class="final-cta"><div class="container"><h2>Have a property in mind?</h2><p>Tell us what you plan to buy and improve. We will review the details and connect you with funding sources without promising an outcome.</p><a class="btn" href="#deal-form">Submit your project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
